  "title": "Two-Bit Controlled Function Generator (X, X+1, X', X'+1)",
  "description": "Design a circuit controlled by two select lines S1 S0 that produces the following output for a 4-bit number X: 00 -> X, 01 -> X + 1, 10 -> X', 11 -> X' + 1. Use XOR gates and ONE 7483 IC only. You are NOT allowed to use any inverter (7404). Here '+' means the addition operation. Hint: X XOR S1 gives X when S1 = 0 and X' when S1 = 1; S0 can be applied to the Carry-In of the 7483 while all B inputs are grounded.",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "design",
